      "<p>Signals: the question asks for a count, a minimum or maximum, or a yes or no on feasibility; choices at each step lead to the same remaining problem; and brute force would be exponential because of repeated work.</p><p>To pick the state I ask: what is the smallest amount of information that determines the answer for the rest of the problem? For a string it is usually an index (or a pair of indices), for money an amount, for items an index plus capacity. Then I write the recurrence in words, find the base cases, decide the order (smaller states first), and read off time as (number of states) x (work per state).</p>",
